to add a formal export ledger to the budget system, not to route exports back into in-tank dissolved pools."}],"summary":"The sole disputed amendment (fr-2-54872de9) is rejected. CleanFilter's reduction of microbe biomass without routing to in-tank pools is documented intentional behavior, not a conservation bug. ROUTING.md explicitly classifies CleanFilter as a maintenance export (lines 146, 163), and the budget system records the mass decrease as a visible negative delta on the action stage. The same export-by-reduction pattern is used by SiphonDetritus, confirming it as the established convention. The amendment's proposed fix of routing to DON/DOC would contradict the design by keeping exported waste in the tank."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"b9c7e9da-a897-48c1-9108-04e064d69a11"}
